f(11,'explanation','Correct. Direct reclaim executes in the allocating context, but flags, cgroup pressure, order and fragmentation determine whether it runs.','NeedGFPconditions.',vm,o=0)
f(11,'workedExample','Watermarks influence background reclaim and allocation reserves, while cgroup limits and allocation constraints can also cause direct reclaim. Correlate stalls with reclaim/compaction tracing and memory PSI; a 50 ms duration alone does not establish the cause. Watermark tuning may help at a capacity cost but is not a universal fix. Free memory alone is insufficient; inspect MemAvailable, cgroup usage and pressure.','Do notdiagnosefromstallsorblindraise.',vm+ps)
